      "writtenOn": "2022-05-16T20:36:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We generally avoid global variables, they make testing difficult.  Each `blueprint.Context` should get its own singleton, which means each call to the factory should return a unique object.  You can make that work by instead of having the module register with the singleton, have the singleton call `SingletonContext.VisitAllModules` and use `SingletonContext.ModuleProvider` to query for a provider struct from each one.  `gen_notice` modules can call `ModuleContext.SetProvider` to export a provider struct.",
