      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T01:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For one, the tools that generate the output will conditionally gzip it base on the file extension. If a blueprint specifies a suffix that doesn\u0027t end in .gz, it would be an error to request zipping and vice versa.\n\nI don\u0027t necessarily agree with your assertion about booleans. I worked on one project where the tactic of using boolean properties led to an awful mess. Not saying that necessarily applies here, but it does suggest at least the \"always\" is suspect.\n\nWe have a hard deadline for 1 instance of this in a week.\n\nAfter we merge the code for that 1 instance, we can change the gzip feature to a separate flag independent of file extension as a separate topic, and introduce the boolean properties in that topic. The 1 existing instance will use the default text format so it\u0027s blueprint won\u0027t need any changes.",
      "parentUuid": "9ba1c08c_2e289680",
      "revId": "5db7e0d4435bcc8e163dfeb70343f1596f650395",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1efd508_54ad87a1",
        "filename": "android/gen_notice.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
