      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T21:37:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am only asking to defer that to a later change topic.\n\nThe principal reason is changing the notice output binaries to use a flag greatly expands the scope. It pulls in another project, and it requires examining and possibly changing everywhere those binaries are currently used.\n\nI wish to defer that work to a later topic so that I can get to work on the tests for the feature now -- before the hard deadline -- and take my time to make that change carefully.\n\nYour earlier comment caused me to learn that stem and suffix properties are idiomatic in Soong. The suffix property suffices for now to control the output format without expanding the scope of the change.\n\nI intentionally did not bother adding support for .htm.gz because that is not a common combination. I will remove support for .htm to avoid that issue.",
      "parentUuid": "c1efd508_54ad87a1",
      "revId": "5db7e0d4435bcc8e163dfeb70343f1596f650395",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "474b1afc_bd2edff3",
        "filename": "android/gen_notice.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T21:51:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not suggesting modifying the notice output binaries, although that would be a reasonable later change.  I\u0027m suggesting modifying the `getSuffix()` method to be:\n\n```\nfunc (m *genNoticeModule) getExtension() string {\n        ext :\u003d \"\"\n\tswitch {\n\tcase proptools.Bool(m.properties.Html):\n\t    ext \u003d \".html\"\n\tcase proptools.Bool(m.properties.Xml):\n\t    ext \u003d \".xml\"\n        default:\n            ext \u003d \".txt\"\n        }\n        if proptools.Bool(m.properties.Gzipped) {\n            ext +\u003d \".gz\"\n        }\n        return ext\n}\n```\n\nThe `suffix` property in other modules is not used to override the extension, it\u0027s used to append to the `stem` property under certain conditions, for example to differentiate between the a 32-bit binary and a 64-bit binary (`dhry32` vs. `dhry64`).",
      "parentUuid": "49b1ff0f_576b1195",
      "revId": "5db7e0d4435bcc8e163dfeb70343f1596f650395",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
